    "details": {
      "isComplex": true,
      "level": {
        "value": 3
      },
      "disable": "<p>@Check[type:medicine|dc:22|name:To Convince the Spirit That Everything is Okay|traits:complex,haunt] (trained) Twice To Convince the Spirit That Nothjing is Wrong,</p>\n<p>@Check[type:occultism|dc:18|name: To Banish Spirit|traits:complex,haunt] (expert) To Banish Spirit,</p>\n<p>@Check[type:religion|dc:18|name: To Banish Spirit|traits:complex,haunt] (expert) To Banish Spirit,</p>\n<p>@Check[type:perception|dc:21|name:To Hear a Fearful Child Ask \"What's on your face Mommy?\"|traits:complex,haunt] (trained)To Hear a Fearful Child Ask \"What's on your face Mommy?\"</p>",
      "description": "<p style=\"text-align:justify\">Suddenly, you feel as if your face had suddenly erupted into a tangled mess of tumors and boils, lasting just long enough for you to attempt to claw the offending sickness from your skull.</p>",
      "reset": "<p>The haunt automatically resets after 1 day until the supernatural fungus in B37 is dealt with, even if the haunt was previously disabled.</p>",
      "routine": "<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Routine:</strong> A creature that fails its will save against Phage Infection must, on their turn in initiative, succeed at a @Check[type:will|dc:25|name:Suggestion|traits:mental,incapacitating,linguistic,necromancy,occult] basic will save or take 2d12 damage as they attempt to claw away the phantom phage on their face- This routine continues until the creature succeeds at two such will saves in a row, is dragged from the room by a successful maneuver, or falls unconscious.&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Festering Haunt: </strong>This haunt only aﬁects those haunted by Voral Foxglove and his painful death by a thousand necromantic diseasess. If no creatures in a group are haunted by Vorel Foxglove, this haunt may target any creature in a group.</p>"
    },
